t after loading, check that user/item IDs map to contiguous indices).\n- Pin dependencies with a requirements.txt or environment file; log versions at runtime.\n- Consider optional parallelization for seeds and consistent RNG usage across processes; aggregate results after runs.\n- Ensure logging includes runtime per run, not just final metrics.\n\n                ", 'Feedback about execution time': '', 'Instructions': {'Response format': 'Your response should be a brief outline/sketch of your proposed solution in natural language (7-10 sentences), followed by a single markdown code block (using the format ```python ... ```) which implements this solution and prints out the evaluation metric(s) if applicable. There should be no additional headings or text in your response. Just natural language text followed by a newline and then the markdown code block. Make sure to write concise code.', 'Improvement guidelines': ['Based on the scoring feedback above, focus on the requirements that need improvement.', 'Your goal is to enhance the implementation while maintaining its working functionality.'], 'Implementation guideline': ['CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS - You should use lenskit as much as possible', 'CRITICAL MODEL INPUT GUIDELINES:', '  - Always pay extra attention to the input to the model being properly normalized', "  - This is extremely important because the input to the model's forward pass directly affects the output, and the loss function is computed based on the output", 'For generative modeling tasks, you must:', '  - Generate a set of samples from your model', '  - Compare these samples with ground truth data using appropriate visualizations', "  - When saving plots, always use the 'working_dir' variable that will be defined at the start of the script", '  - Make sure to give each figure a unique and appropriate name based on the dataset it represents, rather than reusing the same filename.', 'Important code structure requirements:', '  - Do NOT put any execution code inside \'if __name__ == "__main__":\' block', '  - All code should be at the global scope or in functions that are called from the global scope', '  - The script should execute immediately when run, without requiring any special entry point', 'The code should start with:', '  import os', "  working_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')", '  os.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)', 'The code should be a single-file python program that is self-contained and can be executed as-is.', "No parts of the code should be skipped, don't terminate the code execution before finishing the script.", 'Your response should only contain a single code block.', 'Be aware of the running time of the code, it should complete within an hour.', 'You can also use the "./working" directory to store any temporary files that your code needs to create.', 'Data saving requirements:', '- Save all plottable data (metrics, losses, predictions, etc.) as numpy arrays using np.save()', '- Use the following naming convention for saved files:', '  ```python', '  # At the start of your code', '  experiment_data = {', "      'dataset_name_1': {", "          'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []},", "          'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []},", "          'predictions': [],", "          'ground_truth': [],", '          # Add other relevant data', '      },', '      # Add additional datasets as needed:', "      'dataset_name_2': {", "          'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []},", "          'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []},", "          'predictions': [],", "          'ground_truth': [],", '          # Add other relevant data', '      },', '  }', '  # During training/evaluation:', "  experiment_data['dataset_name_1']['metrics']['train'].append(train_metric)", '  ```', '- Include timestamps or epochs with the saved metrics', '- For large datasets, consider saving in chunks or using np.savez_compressed()', 'CRITICAL EVALUATION REQUIREMENTS - Your code MUST include ALL of these:', '  1. Track and print validation loss (if applicable) at each epoch or at suitable intervals:', '     ```python', "     print(f'Epoch {{epoch}}: validation_loss = {{val_loss:.4f}}')", '     ```', '  2. Track and update ALL these additional metrics: None', '  3. Update metrics at EACH epoch:', '  4. Save ALL metrics at the end:', '     ```python', "     np.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data)", '     ```']}, 'Previous solution': {'Code': '```python\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport random\nimport time\nfrom math import log2\n\n# Setup working directory\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n# Data loading\nDATA_PATH = \'u.data\'\nif not os.path.exists(DATA_PATH):\n    raise SystemExit("u.data not found in current directory. Please place MovieLens100K u.data in the working directory.")\n\ncol_names = [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']\ndf = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, sep=\'\\t\', header=None, names=col_names, engine=\'python\')\n# Implicit feedback: keep ratings >= 4 as interactions\ndf = df[df[\'rating\'] >= 4].copy()\ndf[\'user\'] = df[\'user\'].astype(int) - 1\ndf[\'item\'] = df[\'item\'].astype(int) - 1\nn_users = int(df[\'user\'].max()) + 1\nn_items = int(df[\'item\'].max()) + 1\n\n# Fixed split configuration\nTEST_FRAC = 0.2\nSPLIT_SEED = 12345  # fixed across runs\nSEEDS = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\nEPOCHS = 5\nK = 20  # latent factors\nLR = 0.05\nREG = 0.01\nTOP_K = [5, 10, 20]\n\n# Prepare fixed train/test split (deterministic across seeds)\ndef fixed_split_all_users(data, test_frac=TEST_FRAC, split_seed=SPLIT_SEED):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(split_seed)\n    train_pairs = []\n    test_pairs = []\n    gt_per_user = {}\n    for u, group in data.groupby(\'user\'):\n        items = group[\'item\'].values\n        if len(items) == 0:\n            continue\n        idx = rng.permutation(len(items))\n        n_test = max(1, int(len(items) * test_frac))\n        test_items = items[idx[:n_test]]\n        train_items = items[idx[n_test:]]\n        for it in train_items:\n            train_pairs.append((int(u), int(it)))\n        for it in test_items:\n            test_pairs.append((int(u), int(it)))\n            gt_per_user.setdefault(int(u), set()).add(int(it))\n    return train_pairs, test_pairs, gt_per_user\n\ntrain_pairs, test_pairs, gt_per_user = fixed_split_all_users(df, TEST_FRAC, SPLIT_SEED)\n\n# Helpers\ndef logistic(x):\n    return 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-x))\n\n# Training + evaluation helpers (pure SGD MF to ensure epoch-level losses and reproducibility)\n\ndef train_mf_sgd(train_pairs, n_users, n_items, seed, epochs=EPOCHS, lr=LR, reg=REG, k=K, test_pairs=None, gt_per_user=None):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    U = rng.normal(scale=0.1, size=(n_users, k))\n    V = rng.normal(scale=0.1, size=(n_items, k))\n    epoch_losses = []\n    val_ks = [None]*epochs\n    for epoch in range(epochs):\n        order = np.arange(len(train_pairs))\n        rng.shuffle(order)\n        train_loss = 0.0\n        for idx in order:\n            u, i = train_pairs[idx]\n            u_vec = U[u]\n            v_vec = V[i]\n            score = u_vec @ v_vec\n            p = logistic(score)\n            grad = p - 1.0  # positive sample\n            old_u = u_vec.copy()\n            U[u] -= lr * (grad * v_vec + reg * u_vec)\n            V[i] -= lr * (grad * old_u + reg * v_vec)\n            train_loss += -np.log(p + 1e-12)\n        train_loss /= max(1, len(train_pairs))\n        epoch_losses.append(train_loss)\n        # Optional: compute simple validation loss on provided test pairs if given\n        if test_pairs:\n            val_loss = 0.0\n            for (u, i) in test_pairs:\n                score = U[u] @ V[i]\n                p = logistic(score)\n                val_loss += -np.log(p + 1e-12)\n            val_loss /= max(1, len(test_pairs))\n            val_ks[epoch] = val_loss\n        else:\n            val_ks[epoch] = None\n    return U, V, epoch_losses, val_ks\n\n# Ranking metrics (NDCG and Recall) helpers\nimport math\n\ndef compute_ranking_metrics(U, V, test_users, gt_per_user, all_items, top_k_list=[5,10,20]):\n    if len(test_users) == 0:\n        return {k: {"ndcg":0.0, "recall":0.0} for k in top_k_list}\n    ndcg_acc = {k: 0.0 for k in top_k_list}\n    recall_acc = {k: 0.0 for k in top_k_list}\n    count = 0\n    for u in test_users:\n        scores = U[u] @ V.T  # shape (n_items,)\n        # get ranking order (descending)\n        ranked_items = np.argsort(scores)[::-1]\n        gt = gt_per_user.get(int(u), set())\n        if len(gt) == 0:\n            continue\n        # For quick lookup\n        gt_set = set(int(x) for x in gt)\n        for k in top_k_list:\n            topk = ranked_items[:k]\n            # DCG\n            dcg = 0.0\n            for rank, item in enumerate(topk, start=1):\n                if int(item) in gt_set:\n                    dcg += 1.0 / math.log(rank + 1, 2)\n            idcg = sum(1.0 / math.log(r + 1, 2) for r in range(1, min(k, len(gt_set)) + 1))\n            ndcg = dcg / max(idcg, 1e-12)\n            # Recall\n            recall = len([it for it in topk if int(it) in gt_set]) / float(len(gt_set))\n            ndcg_acc[k] += ndcg\n            recall_acc[k] += recall\n        count += 1\n    if count == 0:\n        return {k: {"ndcg":0.0, "recall":0.0} for k in top_k_list}\n    for k in top_k_list:\n        ndcg_acc[k] /= count\n        recall_acc[k] /= count\n    return {k: {"ndcg": ndcg_acc[k], "recall": recall_acc[k]} for k in top_k_list}\n\n# Results collection\nresults_rows = []\nexperiment_data = {\n    \'MovieLens100K_ImplicitMF\': {\n        \'metrics\': {\'val\': []},\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': []},\n        \'predictions\': [],\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\n        \'seed\': None\n    }\n}\nstart_time = time.time()\n\nfor seed in SEEDS:\n    t0 = time.time()\n    # Train with seed (affects initialization/shuffle)\n    U, V, train_epochs_losses, val_per_epoch = train_mf_sgd(\n        train_pairs, n_users, n_items, seed,\n        epochs=EPOCHS, lr=LR, reg=REG, k=K,\n        test_pairs=test_pairs, gt_per_user=gt_per_user\n    )\n    # Final evaluation on test set: ranking metrics\n    test_users = sorted(gt_per_user.keys())\n    metrics = compute_ranking_metrics(U, V, test_users, gt_per_user, np.arange(n_items), top_k_list=TOP_K)\n    # Aggregate per-K\n    ndcg_vals = [metrics[k][\'ndcg\'] for k in TOP_K]\n    recall_vals = [metrics[k][\'recall\'] for k in TOP_K]\n    # Validation loss, per epoch (print)\n    for epoch, v in enumerate(train_epochs_losses, start=1):\n        print(f"Seed {seed} Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS}: training_loss={v:.6f}, val_loss={val_per_epoch[epoch-1] if val_per_epoch[epoch-1] is not None else \'na\'}")\n    # Save per-run results\n    row = {\n        \'run_id\': f\'run_{seed}\',\n        \'seed\': seed,\n    }\n    for idx, k in enumerate(TOP_K):\n        row[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = ndcg_vals[idx]\n        row[f\'recall@{k}\'] = recall_vals[idx]\n    results_rows.append(row)\n    # Store aggregate in experiment_data numpy-friendly format\n    experiment_data[\'MovieLens100K_ImplicitMF\'][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append((seed, val_per_epoch[-1] if val_per_epoch[-1] is not None else None))\n    experiment_data[\'MovieLens100K_ImplicitMF\'][\'losses\'][\'train\'].append((seed, train_epochs_losses))\n    experiment_data[\'MovieLens100K_ImplicitMF\'][\'seed\'] = seed\n    t1 = time.time()\n    print(f"Seed {seed} completed in {t1-t0:.2f} sec. Final ndcg@5/10/20: {ndcg_vals[0]:.4f}, {ndcg_vals[1]:.4f}, {ndcg_vals[2]:.4f}")\n\n# Save results CSV\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results_rows)\nresults_csv_path = os.path.join(working_dir, \'results.csv\')\nresults_df.to_csv(results_csv_path, index=False)\nprint(\'Saved per-run results to\', results_csv_path)\n\n# Save a numpy dump for reproducibility\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data)\nprint(\'Experiment data saved to\', os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'))\n\n# Summary: compute mean and std across seeds for each metric\nsummary = {}\nfor k in TOP_K:\n    mean_ndcg = results_df[f\'ndcg@{k}\'].mean()\n    std_ndcg = results_df[f\'ndcg@{k}\'].std()\n    mean_recall = results_df[f\'recall@{k}\'].mean()\n    std_recall = results_df[f\'recall@{k}\'].std()\n    summary[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = (mean_ndcg, std_ndcg)\n    summary[f\'recall@{k}\'] = (mean_recall, std_recall)\nprint(\'\\nSeed-effect summary (mean ± std):\')\nfor k in TOP_K:\n    m_ndcg, s_ndcg = summary[f\'ndcg@{k}\']\n    m_rec, s_rec = summary[f\'recall@{k}\']\n    print(f\' ndcg@{k}: {m_ndcg:.4f} ± {s_ndcg:.4f} | recall@{k}: {m_rec:.4f} ± {s_rec:.4f}\')\n\n```'}}
