[2026/05/14 13:26:00] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': "You are an expert research assistant responding to the user in a conversational setting. You have access to the code and the experiment output. Your task is to answer the user's request based solely on these materials. Use the code to understand what was tested and the output to determine the results. Do not hallucinate, speculate, or assume any information that is not explicitly contained in the output. If the available information is insufficient, explain the limitation clearly and remain factual.", 'User Request': "I'd like to run an experiment to quantify how much random seeds affect recommender system results.\nPlease use a simple ImplicitMF algorithm from LensKit, perform a train/test split on the MovieLens100K 'u.data',\ntrain it multiple times with identical settings but different random seeds,\nand analyze how metrics like NDCG or Recall vary across runs to find out if reporting seeds is important.\nI placed the 'u.data' file of MovieLens100K in your current working directory. You can load it from there!", 'Experiment Code': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport random\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n\nDATA_PATH = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'u.data')\nSEEDS = list(range(10))\nK = 10\nTEST_SIZE = 0.2\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    'movielens100k': {\n        'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []},\n        'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []},\n        'predictions': [],\n        'ground_truth': [],\n        'seed': [],\n        'recall@k': [],\n        'ndcg@k': [],\n        'timestamp_or_run': [],\n    }\n}\n\ntry:\n    from lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nexcept Exception:\n    from lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\n\ncols = ['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp']\ndf = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, sep='\\t', names=cols, engine='python')\ndf['user'] = df['user'].astype(np.int64)\ndf['item'] = df['item'].astype(np.int64)\ndf['rating'] = df['rating'].astype(np.float32)\n\ntrain_df, test_df = train_test_split(df, test_size=TEST_SIZE, random_state=42)\ncommon_users = np.intersect1d(train_df['user'].unique(), test_df['user'].unique())\ntrain_df = train_df[train_df['user'].isin(common_users)].copy()\ntest_df = test_df[test_df['user'].isin(common_users)].copy()\n\ngt = test_df.groupby('user')['item'].apply(list).to_dict()\ntrain_items = train_df.groupby('user')['item'].apply(set).to_dict()\nall_items = np.sort(df['item'].unique())\ntrain_interactions = train_df[['user', 'item', 'rating']].copy()\ntrain_interactions['rating'] = train_interactions['rating'].astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef rank_metrics(recommended_items, relevant_items, k):\n    recommended_items = list(recommended_items)[:k]\n    rel = set(relevant_items)\n    hits = np.array([1 if item in rel else 0 for item in recommended_items], dtype=np.float32)\n    recall = float(hits.sum() / max(1, len(rel)))\n    if hits.sum() == 0:\n        return recall, 0.0\n    discounts = 1.0 / np.log2(np.arange(2, len(hits) + 2))\n    dcg = float(np.sum(hits * discounts))\n    ideal_len = min(len(rel), k)\n    idcg = float(np.sum(discounts[:ideal_len]))\n    ndcg = float(dcg / idcg) if idcg > 0 else 0.0\n    return recall, ndcg\n\n\ndef recommend_for_user(model, user, candidates, n=K):\n    cand_index = pd.Index(candidates)\n    scores = model.predict_for_user(int(user), cand_index)\n    scores = np.asarray(scores)\n    recs = pd.DataFrame({'item': np.asarray(candidates), 'score': scores})\n    recs = recs.sort_values('score', ascending=False, kind='mergesort')\n    return recs['item'].head(n).tolist()\n\n\ndef fit_implicit_mf(seed):\n    random.seed(seed)\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    trial_kwargs = [\n        dict(features=40, iterations=20, reg=0.1, rng_spec=seed),\n        dict(features=40, iterations=20, reg=0.1, random_state=seed),\n        dict(features=40, iterations=20, reg=0.1),\n    ]\n    last_err = None\n    for kwargs in trial_kwargs:\n        try:\n            model = ImplicitMF(**kwargs)\n            model.fit(train_interactions)\n            return model\n        except Exception as e:\n            last_err = e\n    raise last_err\n\nresults = []\nrecalls, ndcgs = [], []\n\nfor run_idx, seed in enumerate(SEEDS):\n    model = fit_implicit_mf(seed)\n    user_recalls, user_ndcgs = [], []\n    per_user_preds, per_user_gt = [], []\n\n    for user, rel_items in gt.items():\n        seen = train_items.get(user, set())\n        candidates = [it for it in all_items if it not in seen]\n        if not candidates or len(rel_items) == 0:\n            continue\n        top_items = recommend_for_user(model, user, candidates, n=K)\n        recall, ndcg = rank_metrics(top_items, rel_items, K)\n        user_recalls.append(recall)\n        user_ndcgs.append(ndcg)\n        per_user_preds.append(top_items)\n        per_user_gt.append(rel_items)\n\n    mean_recall = float(np.mean(user_recalls)) if user_recalls else 0.0\n    mean_ndcg = float(np.mean(user_ndcgs)) if user_ndcgs else 0.0\n    recalls.append(mean_recall)\n    ndcgs.append(mean_ndcg)\n\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['seed'].append(seed)\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['timestamp_or_run'].append(run_idx)\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['recall@k'].append(mean_recall)\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['ndcg@k'].append(mean_ndcg)\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['metrics']['val'].append([mean_recall, mean_ndcg])\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['predictions'].append(per_user_preds)\n    experiment_data['movielens100k']['ground_truth'].append(per_user_gt)\n    results.append({'seed': seed, 'recall@k': mean_recall, 'ndcg@k': mean_ndcg})\n\n    print(f'Seed {seed}: Recall@{K} = {mean_recall:.4f}, NDCG@{K} = {mean_ndcg:.4f}')\n\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\nrecalls = np.asarray(recalls, dtype=np.float32)\nndcgs = np.asarray(ndcgs, dtype=np.float32)\n\nrecall_mean = recalls.mean()\nrecall_std = recalls.std(ddof=1) if len(recalls) > 1 else 0.0\nndcg_mean = ndcgs.mean()\nndcg_std = ndcgs.std(ddof=1) if len(ndcgs) > 1 else 0.0\nrecall_ci95 = 1.96 * recall_std / np.sqrt(len(recalls)) if len(recalls) > 1 else 0.0\nndcg_ci95 = 1.96 * ndcg_std / np.sqrt(len(ndcgs)) if len(ndcgs) > 1 else 0.0\n\nprint('\\nPer-seed results:')\nprint(results_df.to_string(index=False))\nprint('\\nSummary over seeds:')\nprint(f'Recall@{K}: mean={recall_mean:.4f}, std={recall_std:.4f}, min={recalls.min():.4f}, max={recalls.max():.4f}, 95%CI±{recall_ci95:.4f}')\nprint(f'NDCG@{K}:   mean={ndcg_mean:.4f}, std={ndcg_std:.4f}, min={ndcgs.min():.4f}, max={ndcgs.max():.4f}, 95%CI±{ndcg_ci95:.4f}')\n\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'recall_by_seed.npy'), recalls)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ndcg_by_seed.npy'), ndcgs)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'seeds.npy'), np.asarray(SEEDS))\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'movielens100k_seed_metric_matrix.npy'), np.vstack([recalls, ndcgs]))\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'movielens100k_seed_results_table.npy'), results_df.to_records(index=False))\n\nsummary_path = os.path.join(working_dir, 'movielens100k_seed_sensitivity_summary.txt')\nwith open(summary_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write('MovieLens100K ImplicitMF seed sensitivity\\n')\n    f.write(f'K={K}, test_size={TEST_SIZE}, seeds={SEEDS}\\n')\n    f.write(f'Recall@{K}: mean={recall_mean:.6f}, std={recall_std:.6f}, min={recalls.min():.6f}, max={recalls.max():.6f}, ci95={recall_ci95:.6f}\\n')\n    f.write(f'NDCG@{K}: mean={ndcg_mean:.6f}, std={ndcg_std:.6f}, min={ndcgs.min():.6f}, max={ndcgs.max():.6f}, ci95={ndcg_ci95:.6f}\\n')\n```", 'Experiment Output': '```\nNumba is using threading layer omp - consider TBB\nfound 1 potential runtime problems - see https://boi.st/lkpy-perf\nSeed 0: Recall@10 = 0.1712, NDCG@10 = 0.2353\nSeed 1: Recall@10 = 0.1685, NDCG@10 = 0.2325\nSeed 2: Recall@10 = 0.1685, NDCG@10 = 0.2344\nSeed 3: Recall@10 = 0.1706, NDCG@10 = 0.2354\nSeed 4: Recall@10 = 0.1713, NDCG@10 = 0.2349\nSeed 5: Recall@10 = 0.1748, NDCG@10 = 0.2385\nSeed 6: Recall@10 = 0.1708, NDCG@10 = 0.2335\nSeed 7: Recall@10 = 0.1746, NDCG@10 = 0.2380\nSeed 8: Recall@10 = 0.1750, NDCG@10 = 0.2334\nSeed 9: Recall@10 = 0.1734, NDCG@10 = 0.2375\n\nPer-seed results:\n seed  recall@k   ndcg@k\n    0  0.171221 0.235343\n    1  0.168500 0.232517\n    2  0.168450 0.234391\n    3  0.170568 0.235354\n    4  0.171313 0.234939\n    5  0.174826 0.238498\n    6  0.170845 0.233476\n    7  0.174615 0.237953\n    8  0.175032 0.233378\n    9  0.173395 0.237543\n\nSummary over seeds:\nRecall@10: mean=0.1719, std=0.0025, min=0.1685, max=0.1750, 95%CI±0.0015\nNDCG@10:   mean=0.2353, std=0.0021, min=0.2325, max=0.2385, 95%CI±0.0013\nExecution time: 3 minutes seconds (time limit is an hour).\n```', 'Instructions': ['1. Use the code to interpret what the experiment did and what metrics or results are relevant.', '2. Read the output carefully and extract factual findings that answer the user request.', '3. Formulate your response as if chatting directly with the user — clear, concise, and natural.', '4. Do not output any structured formats or metadata (no JSON, tables, etc.) unless the user request explicitly asks for it.', '5. Be confident, factual, and grounded only in the provided information.', '6. If the experiment output is ambiguous or incomplete, mention this explicitly instead of guessing.']}
