ha is declared as a parameter in the spec but is not configurable; no confidence-based dataset is constructed.\n- Missing interactions handling is unclear; it should create a user-item confidence dataset and exclude missing interactions.\nImprovements:\n- Add a preprocessing step to convert rating -> confidence using a configurable alpha (default 40), e.g., conf = 1 + alpha * rating.\n- Remap user/item IDs to 0-based indices and ensure the same mapping is used across train/test splits.\n- Build a LensKit-compatible RatingDataset (or equivalent) using the implicit confidence values (and ensure missing interactions are excluded).\n\n2) Train/test split strategy (Requirement 2)\n- Per-user holdout is implemented, and the seed controls the per-user splits, which supports reproducibility, but there is no explicit minimum interaction requirements enforcement (or dropping users with insufficient interactions is not enforced).\n- The split function uses a deterministic seed_for_user derived from seed and user_id, which is good, but its deterministic logic could be simplified and documented for reproducibility.\nImprovements:\n- Implement a clear minimum interaction threshold per user (drop users with fewer than min_interactions in either train or test) and document behavior.\n- Ensure the train/test split strictly excludes test data from the training set in the final dataset used for optimization.\n\n3) Repeated experiments with different seeds (Requirement 3)\n- Seeds are provided and used to re-create train/test splits; initialization randomness is attempted by passing seed to the model.\n- However, the per-run RNG seeding is insufficient if LensKit relies on its own RNGs or Python’s random. Also, there is no reproducibility test across runs beyond the splits.\nImprovements:\n- Explicitly seed Python random and NumPy RNGs for each run; ensure LensKit’s RNG (if accessible) is seeded using the same seed.\n- Add a reproducibility check or a small log of the per-run seeds and